---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { t } from '../i18n';
import { resolvePageSeo } from '../config/seo';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import ContactSupportSection from '../components/ContactSupportSection.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema, webPageSchema } from '../utils/schema';

const seo = resolvePageSeo('/support/');
const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Support', path: '/support/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={seo.title}
  description={seo.description}
  logoAlt="Support – site logo"
  jsonLd={[
    webPageSchema({
      name: seo.title,
      description: seo.description,
      url: '/support/',
    }),
    breadcrumbSchema(breadcrumbs),
  ]}
>
  <section class="border-b border-border bg-muted/20 py-8 md:py-10">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5">
      <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <ContactSupportSection titleId="support-page-title" showTicketTips />

  <article class="content-markdown border-t border-border bg-muted/10 py-10 md:py-12">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5">
      <h2>What this site can and cannot fix</h2>
      <p>
        {t.site.domain} publishes pricing summaries, ESP module overviews, and PC requirement checklists. We route
        checkout through partner <a href="/go/">product checkout bridges</a> but do not issue license keys, reset HWID
        bans, or walk through loader injection steps.
      </p>
      <p>
        When your question is about activation errors, payment disputes on the partner receipt, or Cloud DMA guest
        setup, open a ticket with the vendor named on your order confirmation—not with this domain unless the issue is
        a broken guide link or affiliate disclosure.
      </p>

      <h2>Self-serve answers before you email</h2>
      <p>
        Filter the <a href="/faq/">Aion Classic pre-checkout FAQ</a> for plan, ESP, and Cloud DMA topics. Compare
        listed $35 monthly and $150 lifetime figures on the
        <a href="/aion-classic-pricing/">ESP and aimbot price breakdown</a>, then read the
        <a href="/aion-classic-esp/">main-plan feature summary</a> if you are unsure which modules ship together.
      </p>
      <p>
        Cloud DMA buyers should read the <a href="/cloud-dma-for-aion-classic/">Cloud DMA listing summary</a> and the
        <a href="/guides/cloud-dma-setup/">step-zero setup checklist</a> before opening vendor tickets about GREENWARD,
        Static Server, or AWS billing.
      </p>

      <h2>Information to paste into vendor tickets</h2>
      <p>
        Vendors typically need your order ID, whether you bought monthly or lifetime ESP access, Windows edition (Home vs
        Pro), and whether HVCI, TPM, Secure Boot, and firmware virtualization are enabled. Capture the exact error text
        from the loader or Hyper-V guest instead of paraphrasing.
      </p>
      <p>
        For hardware checklist language you can copy, use the
        <a href="/aion-classic-system-requirements/">Windows and Cloud DMA requirement tables</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Response times and refunds</h2>
      <p>
        Vendor Discord or ticket queues may be slower on patch days. License email can land in spam folders—search for
        the partner domain before requesting a resend.
      </p>
      <p>
        Chargebacks and refund windows follow the checkout partner policy printed on your receipt. This site cannot
        override those terms.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>